{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Naphtali is a hind let loose.</b> Swift as hinds when they bound from the war to bring good and choice tidings of victory in battle. That is <b>he gives words of beauty</b>. And so it says: 'and Naphtali upon the heights of the field' — like the runners who run upon mountain heights. And there are those who say: 'Naphtali is a hind' — <b>אילה</b> means a plain, like <b>איל פארן</b>; or alternatively it means a tree, like <b>אילי הצדק</b>." "<b>Let loose.</b> Like planted; like 'her branches went forth, crossed the sea.'" "<b>Words of beauty.</b> In the sense of branches, like 'two or three grains on the top of <b>אמיר</b>' — meaning that the plain of his land will be planted with branches that yield fine and choice fruits."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:17.177415612Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}